{"source":"u-2.5s-cap15-combined-table.tex","caption":"Retrieval from cluttered compartments under clean and noisy observations. Matched comparisons evaluate the effect of retrospective correction under noise.","note":"Protocol: Replanning every 2.5 s; 15° tilt cap; n = 10 scenes per object count and placement difficulty. Clean uses exact object states; Noisy uses 2 cm position noise and 13° rotation noise. Collision avoidance uses ε = 5 mm. Variants: Ours w/o dist. obj. removes the disturbance objective while retaining the constraints. Under noise, Corr. Off directly overwrites the current state with the observation; Corr. On uses the noise-trained retrospective corrector. Metrics: Success requires the target to leave the cabinet without any bystander being pushed out or toppled. Disturbance is final displacement summed over bystanders remaining in the compartment. Bold marks the best success rate across methods under clean observations, or within each matched correction pair under noise (ties included). At 20 objects, Ours uses half the disturbance weights used for 5 and 10 objects.","counts":[5,10,20],"difficulties":["Easy","Hard"],"columns":[{"count":5,"difficulty":"Easy"},{"count":5,"difficulty":"Hard"},{"count":10,"difficulty":"Easy"},{"count":10,"difficulty":"Hard"},{"count":20,"difficulty":"Easy"},{"count":20,"difficulty":"Hard"}],"panels":[{"key":"a","title":"(a) Retrieval success and translational disturbance","metrics":[{"key":"success","label":"Success rate","better":"up","unit":""},{"key":"translation","label":"Translational disturbance","better":"down","unit":"cm"}],"rows":[{"method":"Direct retrieval","observation":"Clean","correction":"–","starred":false,"shaded":false,"values":{"success":[0.6,0.6,0.3,0.2,0.2,0.1],"translation":[26.9,21.5,46.0,48.4,91.2,69.6]},"bold":{"success":[false,false,false,false,false,false],"translation":[false,false,false,false,false,false]}},{"method":"Collision avoidance","observation":"Clean","correction":"–","starred":fa